    "features_html": "<h2>The Short Version</h2>\n<p>Here is what stood out most when we played <strong>Rummy 77</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n    <li><strong>Clean lobby and fast matchmaking:</strong> a table is usually ready within seconds.</li>\n    <li><strong>One-tap Sort:</strong> cards are grouped by suit and color, which makes spotting sequences and sets much easier.</li>\n    <li><strong>Reliable touch controls:</strong> dragging and discarding respond without lag, even when the turn timer is running down.</li>\n    <li><strong>Smooth, light performance:</strong> the game stays steady on newer and older phones, with low battery use and no noticeable heat.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Bottom Line</h2>\n<p>The interface is simple, and that is the point. <strong>Rummy 77</strong> puts classic 13-card rummy first and leaves out the distractions, which makes it a dependable pick for anyone who just wants to play a proper game.</p>",
