    "description": "Developed by Nexus Card Studios, OK Rummy (v1.09.3, 45 MB) turns conventional card matching into a peaceful, solo puzzle-solving adventure. The title removes countdown timers, lobbies, and internet requirements, allowing players to clear patterned boards through logical sets and runs completely at their own speed. Holding a 4.2/5 rating, it is a lightweight, ad-supported brain teaser built purely for casual offline entertainment.",
    "ceo_description": "Transparency & Security Analyst",
    "is_pinned": false,
    "description_html": "<div>\n  <p><strong>OK Rummy: Transforming Classic Card Strategy into a Solo Puzzle Adventure</strong></p>\n\n  <p>Most modern card platforms focus on intense tables, fast clocks, and competitive player pools. Nexus Card Studios takes a deliberate step in the opposite direction with <strong>OK Rummy</strong>, transforming traditional card-matching rules into a single-player logic puzzle.</p>\n\n  <p>At a compact <strong>45 MB</strong>, the game runs smoothly across standard Android hardware without exhausting internal storage or battery life.</p>\n\n  <hr>\n\n  <p><strong>Core Gameplay Mechanics</strong></p>\n  <p>Instead of dealing against live opponents, the game treats card arrangements like interactive puzzles:</p>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li><strong>Board-Clearing Strategy:</strong> Stages present layered, interlocking formations of exposed and hidden cards. Players must dismantle the layout by organizing available cards into valid suits, runs, and sets.</li>\n    <li><strong>Controlled Draw Deck:</strong> Every level gives you a strictly limited draw pile. Drawing without a plan quickly depletes your options, requiring users to look multiple moves ahead to uncover buried cards.</li>\n    <li><strong>Progressive Map Journey:</strong> Clearing boards earns virtual stars that unlock new zones across an illustrated progression map, introducing fresh visual themes and deeper logic puzzles as you advance.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <hr>\n\n  <p><strong>Designed for Thoughtful Play</strong></p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><strong>Timer-Free Environment:</strong> Without turn clocks or aggressive leaderboards, the experience is completely self-paced, making it an effective choice for unwinding.</li>\n    <li><strong>Reliable Offline Access:</strong> The main campaign is fully playable without Wi-Fi or cellular network access, making it dependable during commutes or flights.</li>\n    <li><strong>Helpful Move Assists:</strong> When layouts become congested, built-in undo actions and contextual hints help players navigate tough spots without forcing a full restart.</li>\n    <li><strong>Balanced Free Model:</strong> OK Rummy is entirely free to download and navigate, utilizing non-intrusive video ads between stages rather than paywalled content gates.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <hr>\n\n  <p>With a verified safety profile and a <strong>4.2 out of 5.0 rating</strong>, OK Rummy provides card enthusiasts with a focused, relaxing alternative that prioritizes patience and strategy over fast-paced competition.</p>\n</div>",
    "sync_to_public": true,
    "is_new": false,
    "content": "<div>\n  <p><strong>OK Rummy: Transforming Classic Card Strategy into a Solo Puzzle Adventure</strong></p>\n\n  <p>Most modern card platforms focus on intense tables, fast clocks, and competitive player pools. Nexus Card Studios takes a deliberate step in the opposite direction with <strong>OK Rummy</strong>, transforming traditional card-matching rules into a single-player logic puzzle.</p>\n\n  <p>At a compact <strong>45 MB</strong>, the game runs smoothly across standard Android hardware without exhausting internal storage or battery life.</p>\n\n  <hr>\n\n  <p><strong>Core Gameplay Mechanics</strong></p>\n  <p>Instead of dealing against live opponents, the game treats card arrangements like interactive puzzles:</p>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li><strong>Board-Clearing Strategy:</strong> Stages present layered, interlocking formations of exposed and hidden cards. Players must dismantle the layout by organizing available cards into valid suits, runs, and sets.</li>\n    <li><strong>Controlled Draw Deck:</strong> Every level gives you a strictly limited draw pile. Drawing without a plan quickly depletes your options, requiring users to look multiple moves ahead to uncover buried cards.</li>\n    <li><strong>Progressive Map Journey:</strong> Clearing boards earns virtual stars that unlock new zones across an illustrated progression map, introducing fresh visual themes and deeper logic puzzles as you advance.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <hr>\n\n  <p><strong>Designed for Thoughtful Play</strong></p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><strong>Timer-Free Environment:</strong> Without turn clocks or aggressive leaderboards, the experience is completely self-paced, making it an effective choice for unwinding.</li>\n    <li><strong>Reliable Offline Access:</strong> The main campaign is fully playable without Wi-Fi or cellular network access, making it dependable during commutes or flights.</li>\n    <li><strong>Helpful Move Assists:</strong> When layouts become congested, built-in undo actions and contextual hints help players navigate tough spots without forcing a full restart.</li>\n    <li><strong>Balanced Free Model:</strong> OK Rummy is entirely free to download and navigate, utilizing non-intrusive video ads between stages rather than paywalled content gates.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <hr>\n\n  <p>With a verified safety profile and a <strong>4.2 out of 5.0 rating</strong>, OK Rummy provides card enthusiasts with a focused, relaxing alternative that prioritizes patience and strategy over fast-paced competition.</p>\n</div>",
