    "seo_title": "Maha Games – Gravity Puzzle Game by Jagoan K3",
    "title": "Maha Games – Gravity Puzzle Game by Jagoan K3",
    "author": "Team",
    "is_pinned": false,
    "is_new": false,
    "category": "Yono Apps",
    "description": "Maha Games is a physics-based puzzle game by Jagoan K3. Manipulate gravity, solve creative challenges, and explore immersive puzzle worlds.",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-28T12:38:02.020Z",
    "seo_description": "Maha Games is a physics-based puzzle game by Jagoan K3 featuring gravity, creative challenges, and offline gameplay.",
    "description_html": "<ul>\n  <li><strong>Maha Games:</strong> A Gravity-Bending Puzzle Game Built to Challenge Your Brain</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Maha Games is a physics-based mobile puzzle game developed by Jagoan K3, offering players a unique gameplay experience centered around gravity, momentum, environmental logic, and creative problem-solving.</p>\n\n<p>Unlike conventional mobile puzzle games, Maha Games places players inside floating isometric puzzle environments where manipulating gravity becomes the key to solving increasingly challenging rooms. Players can shift gravity, move objects, use momentum, and create chain reactions to guide an energy orb toward its destination.</p>\n\n<h2>Gravity Is the Main Tool</h2>\n\n<p>The central feature of Maha Games is its gravity-based puzzle system. Players can change the direction of gravity through screen gestures, allowing objects to fall toward ceilings, move across walls, and interact with the surrounding environment in unexpected ways.</p>\n\n<p>Heavy objects can also be used to generate momentum and move lighter objects across gaps or through obstacles. This physics-focused approach encourages players to experiment with different solutions rather than simply following a predetermined sequence of moves.</p>\n\n<h3>A Puzzle Experience Focused on Logic and Creativity</h3>\n\n<p>Maha Games emphasizes spatial reasoning and environmental problem-solving rather than fast reflexes. Players need to observe the three-dimensional puzzle environment, understand how objects will react when gravity changes, and plan their moves accordingly.</p>\n\n<p>The sandbox-style design also encourages experimentation. Players can test unusual approaches, reset a puzzle when necessary, and continue experimenting until they discover a successful solution.</p>\n\n<h3>The Zenith Portal Adds a Changing Challenge</h3>\n\n<p>One of the game's highlighted features is the Zenith Portal, a daily challenge environment designed around changing physics rules.</p>\n\n<p>The changing mechanics can introduce different gameplay conditions, giving players an additional reason to return and experiment with new puzzle configurations.</p>\n\n<h3>A Clean, Immersive Visual Experience</h3>\n\n<p>The game uses floating isometric structures against a deep-space background, creating the appearance of a miniature universe contained inside the player's device.</p>\n\n<p>Its interface is designed around the puzzle environment rather than crowded menus, keeping attention focused on the gameplay and physics interactions.</p>\n\n<p>Haptic feedback is also used to make interactions feel more physical. Different object movements are represented through varying tactile responses, adding another layer to the game's physics-oriented presentation.</p>\n\n<h3>Relaxed Puzzle Solving</h3>\n\n<p>The main campaign is designed without stressful countdown timers, allowing players to spend time analyzing each environment and planning their next move.</p>\n\n<p>An instant rewind function also allows players to restore a puzzle to its starting state, making experimentation easier without requiring lengthy resets or loading screens.</p>\n\n<h3>Small Download Size and Offline Gameplay</h3>\n\n<p>According to the supplied RummyDex information, Maha Games has a compact download size of approximately 35 MB and is listed as version 1.05v.</p>\n\n<p>The main puzzle campaign is described as playable offline, allowing players to solve its physics-based challenges without requiring a continuous Wi-Fi or cellular connection.</p>\n\n<p>The game is listed with an Everyone 10+ rating.</p>\n\n<h3>Free-to-Play Gameplay</h3>\n\n<p>Maha Games is described as free to download and play. The supplied information states that advertising is used between major puzzle levels, while progression is primarily based on the number of puzzle rooms completed.</p>\n\n<h3>Maha Games Ratings and Player Feedback</h3>\n\n<p>The supplied RummyDex information reports ratings from players highlighting aspects such as fluid gameplay, clean layouts, intuitive rules, responsive controls, smooth interface transitions, and quick table interactions.</p>\n\n<p>Some feedback also includes requests for additional customization and features such as more themes and a low-power mode.</p>\n\n<h3>Maha Games at a Glance</h3>\n\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>App Name:</strong> Maha Games</li>\n  <li><strong>Developer:</strong> Jagoan K3</li>\n  <li><strong>Genre:</strong> Physics-based Puzzle</li>\n  <li><strong>Version:</strong> 1.05v</li>\n  <li><strong>Size:</strong> Approximately 35 MB</li>\n  <li><strong>Rating:</strong> Everyone 10+</li>\n  <li><strong>Gameplay:</strong> Gravity, physics, momentum and environmental puzzles</li>\n  <li><strong>Main Campaign:</strong> Offline gameplay</li>\n  <li><strong>Monetization:</strong> Free-to-play with advertisements</li>\n  <li><strong>Highlighted Feature:</strong> Gravity manipulation</li>\n  <li><strong>Additional Feature:</strong> Zenith Portal daily challenge</li>\n  <li><strong>Platform:</strong> Mobile</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Final Take</h3>\n\n<p>Maha Games takes a different approach to mobile puzzle gaming by making gravity and physics the foundation of its challenges. Instead of relying primarily on speed, the game asks players to observe their surroundings, predict physical interactions, experiment with different possibilities, and construct their own solutions.</p>\n\n<p>For players interested in physics-based puzzles, spatial challenges, and relaxed problem-solving, Maha Games presents a distinctive mobile gaming concept centered around one simple idea: change the rules of gravity and find a way through.</p>",
